Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/view/View.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0): a hardware
layer above a WebView is drawn without its drawing cache.

Why: Minato's windows draw in software (ADR-0043 decision 2), where AOSP's View.draw puts a view with a hardware layer
(setLayerType(LAYER_TYPE_HARDWARE), or an animation's withLayer) through its drawing cache, a Bitmap canvas. A WebView's
page lies in the host's view below the window and shows through the area the WebView's onDraw clears; under such a
layer that area is cleared in the cache's bitmap only, which is then drawn over the window's background, so the page
stays covered. On Android the WebView draws the page itself, into the hardware layer, and it shows.

What: a view with a hardware layer that has a WebView with an open host below it (WebViewHoles.above) is drawn as one
without a layer. The layer's paint (setLayerPaint: a color filter, a blend mode) does not apply there, a named
difference; its alpha still does, through saveLayerAlpha. Every other view is drawn as AOSP draws it.

--- a/core/java/android/view/View.java
+++ b/core/java/android/view/View.java
@@ -24558,7 +24558,12 @@
         RenderNode renderNode = null;
         Bitmap cache = null;
         int layerType = getLayerType(); // TODO: signify cache state with just 'cache' local
-        if (layerType == LAYER_TYPE_SOFTWARE || !drawingWithRenderNode) {
+        if (layerType == LAYER_TYPE_HARDWARE && !drawingWithRenderNode
+                && com.android.internal.minato.webkit.WebViewHoles.above(this)) {
+            // Minato: a hardware layer over a WebView whose page shows through a hole in the window is drawn
+            // directly: in a drawing cache the hole would be cleared in the cache's bitmap only.
+            layerType = LAYER_TYPE_NONE;
+        } else if (layerType == LAYER_TYPE_SOFTWARE || !drawingWithRenderNode) {
              if (layerType != LAYER_TYPE_NONE) {
                  // If not drawing with RenderNode, treat HW layers as SW
                  layerType = LAYER_TYPE_SOFTWARE;
